a bias-shaped reduction sinks q then r below o, and nothing else: true
a two-loop bias reduction sinks its one reduction loop below o: true
a reduction already innermost gets no interchange: true
an accumulator a reduction loop's affine index also moves is left alone: true
an overwrite (no self-read) is not an accumulation and is left alone: true
a bf16 accumulator its backend widens to f32 is left alone: true
the same bf16 accumulator kept at its storage precision is sunk (the control): true
admitted, the widened bf16 accumulator is sunk by the chain it gets at its storage precision: true
on CUDA/HIP the untuned compile sinks a segment with the seeding off: true
on CUDA/HIP the sunk routine compiles without falling back to the default: true
on CUDA/HIP the default renders some accumulation against its cell: true
on CUDA/HIP the sunk routine renders fewer accumulations against their cells: true
off CUDA/HIP nothing is sunk: true
with the seeding off nothing is seeded: true
the bias gradient is not trivially zero: true
the fixture is order-sensitive: a reversed f32 reduction differs from it in some cell: true
the sunk bias gradient is bitwise the default pipeline's: true
the sunk weight gradient is bitwise the default pipeline's: true
reduction_sink:false sinks nothing: true
that routine computes the default pipeline's bias gradient: true
